<h2 id="experience">Experience</h2>

<h3 class="experience-header" id="amazon-web-services--8-years">Amazon Web Services — 8 years</h3>

<p>I build query languages, compliance frameworks, and autonomous engineering systems at AWS scale. Three threads run through my work: <strong>making complex systems accessible through language design</strong>, <strong>shifting enforcement left into infrastructure</strong>, and <strong>applying AI agents to accelerate the entire development lifecycle</strong>.</p>

<p class="role"><strong>Observability Query Language &amp; Compiler Design</strong> — CloudWatch Logs (2022–present)</p>

<p>I own feature development for ScrollQL, the query compiler powering CloudWatch Logs Insights — the primary log analysis surface for millions of AWS customers. I design and ship language primitives (aggregation functions, query commands, macro rewrite rules) and led Lookup Tables from design through GA across 32 AWS regions — a new query-time enrichment capability that lets customers join log data against external reference tables without leaving the Insights console.</p>

<p class="role"><strong>Autonomous Software Engineering Systems</strong> (2025–present)</p>

<p>I designed Forge — a self-correcting autonomous pipeline that takes a feature specification and produces a shipped, reviewed code change with zero manual intervention. The system orchestrates workspace provisioning, compiler implementation, test generation, code review submission, and iterative repair from static analysis feedback. First end-to-end run delivered a production ScrollQL feature in under 5 hours. This work directly informs my research on multi-agent system observability.</p>

<p class="role"><strong>Infrastructure Compliance at Scale</strong> — AWS CloudFormation (2018–2022)</p>

<p>I led CloudFormation Hooks from concept to GA — a pre-provisioning compliance framework that lets organizations enforce governance policies before any resource is created. I built the Registry Service for third-party resource type publishing, and drove both systems across all AWS partitions (commercial, GovCloud, China, isolated regions). The resource provider framework I contributed to is used by hundreds of AWS service teams. This work shaped my thinking on how to build extensible, policy-driven systems that operate reliably across trust boundaries.</p>

<h3 class="role" id="research">Research</h3>

<p>My independent research bridges distributed systems and AI — treating multi-agent LLM systems as distributed systems that need the same observability, reliability contracts, and operational rigor we’ve built for microservices over two decades. Two papers in progress; details in <a href="#publications">Publications</a>.</p>

